  "cap_proof": "Original continuous survival has everybasket<140, hence the Asian spot average<140, positive strike100 payoff<40 and discount<1. Independently audited actual digital fully monitored discounted payoff is nonnegative<40. Thus |Yc-Yd|<=40.",
  "proof": "Let D1 be the event that the original continuous and digital strict date1 basket<H decisions differ. Let E1 be any of the first three radial uniforms below delta=2^-20. C06 proves |B_d-B_c|<=eta on E1 complement including native exp and clipping. Therefore D1 intersect E1 complement is contained in the unconditional continuous event |B_c-140|<=eta. Both ORIGINAL fully monitored discounted payoffs Yc and Yd lie in [0,40]; hence E[|Yc-Yd|1{D1 intersect E1 complement}]<=40*P(band), and E[|Yc-Yd|1{D1 intersect E1}]<=40*P(E1)<=40*3*delta. These give only the contribution on D1. The contribution on D1 complement remains unbounded here; in particular later-date switches and smooth Asian payoff discrepancy are unresolved. A whole-B4 radial bad-event tail bound40*30*delta is listed separately and is not added to the date1 bad-event term. No good-event conditioned Gaussian law is asserted.",
